WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.790
Dreamworks' all-singing, all-dancing trolls
are back in a holiday special, which finds

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.590
Poppy, Branch, and friends on a mission to
create a new day of celebration for the Bergens.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.330
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm going to reveal some cool details

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.790
and easter eggs you may have missed in the
Trolls Holiday special.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.460
And I'm running a Trolls book giveaway on
this video.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.489
To enter, make sure you're a subscriber and
leave a comment below about the Trolls movie

00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:25.489
or special.

00:00:25.489 --> 00:00:30.610
When the Cater-bus falls into a wormhole,
there's a lovely easter egg to the original

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.100
Troll toys that these animated characters
are based on.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.470
Biggie, Branch, and Poppy all turn into little
plastic trolls, like the troll toys that were

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:42.220
so popular in the 1960s and again in the 1980s
&amp; 90s.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.890
And Guy Diamond turns into a little plastic
troll covered in glitter, which is funny because

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:51.400
the character of Guy Diamond, who's naked
except for glitter, was created as a tribute

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.590
to the original troll dolls which often didn't
wear any clothes.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:01:00.250
As for Cooper, he turns into a giraffe troll
toy just like the original set of animal trolls

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.780
that were the inspiration for the design of
his character in the movie!

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.190
Later in the special, there's another shout-out
to the original troll toys when Poppy and

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.940
Branch sing a song suggesting a whole range
of holidays the Bergens might like to celebrate.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.330
Among those holidays is Good Luck Troll Day
which involves putting a gem in your belly

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.330
button.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:21.810
This is a little tribute to Thomas Dam, the
Danish creator of the original troll dolls,

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:27.590
who named his toys Good Luck Trolls, and it's
also a hat-tip to the 1990s toys called Treasure

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:31.810
Trolls which had a little jewel in their tummy
button which you could make a wish on.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.590
When the Caterbus crash-lands in front of
King Gristle's castle, the next thing we see

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.380
is loads of butterflies fluttering away.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.080
And those butterflies are the same colours
as the Caterpillar that took Poppy and her

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.870
friends to Bergentown, which is a nice touch
because, in real life, caterpillars do transform

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:48.970
into butterflies.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:54.440
And, in case you missed that, another Caterpillar
explodes into butterflies during the Troll-A-Bration.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:59.900
By the way, something similar happened in
the first Trolls movie when the DJ Stage Bug

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:06.020
burst into a mass of butterflies while Poppy
was giving out invitations to the Trolls party.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.830
There's lots of cool little details on the
Caterbus Express.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:13.220
For example, if you look at Cloud Guy, you'll
notice he's wearing a blue driver cap which

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.609
has a cloud on it that's the same shape as
he is.

00:02:15.609 --> 00:02:20.269
And the controls on the bus's dashboard are
similar to the bug defibrillators that Branch

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:24.209
used to bring Poppy back to life after she
was attacked by spiders in the first movie.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:29.620
The Holiday special also has a few little
reminders from the Trolls movie of King Gristle's

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.540
first date with Bridget, aka Lady Glitter
Sparkles.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.349
First of all, there's a pepperoni pizza lying
around the throne room.

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:40.570
And, like their first date, which they spent
at Captain Starkfunkles Roller Rink, they

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:46.029
also end up skating in Trolls Holiday, though
this time, as it's winter, they go ice rather

00:02:46.029 --> 00:02:47.689
than roller-skating.

00:02:47.689 --> 00:02:51.189
Unlike the Troll Tree in the movie, if you
look closely at the Troll Tree in the Holiday

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:56.030
Special, you can see that it's shaped like
a classic troll's hair, just like in Poppy's

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.069
Holiday presentation to Bridget and Gristle.

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:03.260
And speaking of hair, the top of Bridget's
throne in the Bergen castle has a similar

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.349
shape to the hairstyle she had as Lady Glitter
Sparkles.

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:12.169
To sell their various holiday ideas to Bridget
and Gristle, Poppy and Branch dress up in

00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:15.159
crazy costumes and perform a song-and-dance
routine.

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:19.909
This sequence is a hat-tip to Branch's voice
actor Justin Timberlake and his many Saturday

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:24.700
Night Live skits playing a guy who sells everything
from vegan food to wrapping paper while singing

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.439
and dancing in crazy outfits.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:31.419
There was actually also a nod to Timberlake's
SNL sketches in the Trolls feature film when

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:35.699
Poppy did a song and dance dressed up in a
basket costume, wearing white gloves.

00:03:35.699 --> 00:03:41.159
The only time Biggie's pet worm, Mr Dinkles,
speaks in the feature film is when they discover

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:46.790
Creek is alive, and instead of reacting with
his usual squeaky-voiced 'mew' sound, he says,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.049
'Oh, snap', in a deep voice.

00:03:49.049 --> 00:03:53.309
In that movie, Mr Dinkles was voiced by the
film's director Walt Dohrn, who also voices

00:03:53.309 --> 00:03:58.499
Cloud Guy, but because Mr Dinkles has a bigger
role in the Holiday special, he's now voiced

00:03:58.499 --> 00:04:01.059
by prolific voice actor Kevin Michael Richardson.

00:04:01.059 --> 00:04:05.949
By the way, in the final scene the words 'Happy
holidays to all, and to all, a good night'

00:04:05.949 --> 00:04:09.950
are a spin on the last line of the popular
poem, 'A Visit from St Nicholas', which is

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.430
also known by its famous first line, 'Twas
the night before Christmas.'

